# Mondo Gecko: "{1}, Discard a card: Until end of turn, Mondo Gecko becomes the color of your choice and gains hexproof from
# that color" (CR 105.3, 702.11d), and "Whenever Mondo Gecko deals combat damage to a player, draw a card for each color among
# permanents you control" (CR 105.2). Bot1 discards an Island and makes Mondo red: Bot2's Lightning Bolt can't target it
# (refused). The colors among Bot1's permanents are then red (Mondo, no longer blue) and green (Llanowar Elves): two cards
# when it connects, Bot2 going from 20 to 18. At the end of turn it is blue again.

[Bot1 Deck]
Black Lotus
Mox Jet
Mondo Gecko
Forest
Llanowar Elves
Island x15

[Bot2 Deck]
Mox Ruby
Lightning Bolt
Island x18

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Black Lotus.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Jet.Cast
Bot1.Battlefield.Black Lotus.Activate(Color: Blue)
Bot1.Hand.Mondo Gecko.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
[T2 Bot2.Main1]
Bot2.Hand.Mox Ruby.Cast
[T3 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Hand.Forest.Play
Bot1.Battlefield.Forest.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Llanowar Elves.Cast
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Jet.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mondo Gecko.Activate
Bot1.Colors(Red)
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
? Bot1.Battlefield.Mondo Gecko.Colors = Red
! Bot2.Hand.Lightning Bolt.Cast(Bot1.Battlefield.Mondo Gecko)
Bot1.Attack(Mondo Gecko > Bot2)
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
? Bot1.Hand.Count = 4
[T4 Bot2.Main1]
? Bot1.Battlefield.Mondo Gecko.Colors = Blue

[Expect]
Bot2.Life = 18
